1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,161
Three sigma is not a matter of taste. It

2
00:00:03,261 --> 00:00:06,260
is a bet, and we can price it exactly.

3
00:00:06,350 --> 00:00:10,228
Level one told us which distribution every subgroup

4
00:00:10,328 --> 00:00:14,050
mean is drawn from, assuming nothing has changed.

5
00:00:14,133 --> 00:00:19,254
That curve is the null hypothesis. Not an assumption about the

6
00:00:19,354 --> 00:00:23,801
parts, but a claim about the process: it is unchanged.

7
00:00:23,900 --> 00:00:27,834
So put a pair of limits on it and sweep them outward

8
00:00:27,934 --> 00:00:32,023
from the centre. The readout is not a table: it is the

9
00:00:32,123 --> 00:00:37,144
integral of that curve between the limits, evaluated as they move.

10
00:00:37,233 --> 00:00:42,239
Ninety nine point seven three percent. Nobody chose that number.

11
00:00:42,339 --> 00:00:45,989
It is what plus and minus three sigma is worth.

12
00:00:46,083 --> 00:00:50,427
Everything the process should ever do lives inside. The whole

13
00:00:50,527 --> 00:00:53,414
of the rest is out here in the tails, and

14
00:00:53,514 --> 00:00:56,255
at this scale you cannot see it at all.

15
00:00:56,350 --> 00:01:00,289
So stretch the vertical axis and let them grow. The peak

16
00:01:00,389 --> 00:01:03,968
goes straight out of frame — that is the point. The

17
00:01:04,068 --> 00:01:08,658
tails are seventy times smaller than anything else on this chart.

18
00:01:08,750 --> 00:01:11,154
Each wing is one tenth of one percent

19
00:01:11,254 --> 00:01:13,930
of everything, and there are two of them.

20
00:01:14,016 --> 00:01:18,524
Together they are the tail integral, and it has a closed form.

21
00:01:18,616 --> 00:01:23,148
Evaluate it: zero point zero zero two seven.

22
00:01:23,233 --> 00:01:26,061
Which is the two wings added together.

23
00:01:26,150 --> 00:01:30,401
Invert it and the bet is priced. Zero point two seven

24
00:01:30,501 --> 00:01:35,819
percent is one false alarm in three hundred and seventy subgroups.

25
00:01:35,919 --> 00:01:39,514
A point outside the limit is that bet, taken.

26
00:01:41,100 --> 00:01:43,724
A control chart is simply that same

27
00:01:43,824 --> 00:01:47,072
test, run again on every subgroup, forever.

28
00:01:47,166 --> 00:01:51,218
The limits are the boundary we just drew, turned on its side.

29
00:01:51,316 --> 00:01:56,537
Every point inside is the process agreeing with the null hypothesis.

30
00:01:56,637 --> 00:02:00,840
This is what boring looks like, and boring is the goal.

31
00:02:00,933 --> 00:02:03,353
Then one point steps outside.

32
00:02:03,450 --> 00:02:07,265
Four point one sigma above the centre line, where the

33
00:02:07,365 --> 00:02:11,846
null hypothesis allows one point in three hundred and seventy.

34
00:02:11,933 --> 00:02:16,273
So this is not a bad part, and scrapping it changes nothing.

35
00:02:16,366 --> 00:02:20,830
It is evidence against the hypothesis that nothing changed. The

36
00:02:20,930 --> 00:02:24,018
correct response is to go and find what did.

